1
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:29,337
Every time the rain no longer
falls, and I see the sky?

2
00:00:29,420 --> 00:00:32,277
I think back to when I was a child.

3
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:34,937
Who could only cry?

4
00:00:35,020 --> 00:00:37,597
Blindly chasing after him.

5
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:42,317
I fell far behind my only thought.

6
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:45,417
One day I will be stronger!

7
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:47,897
Bridery and gratitude.

8
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:50,497
Fading with the wind.

9
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:53,317
Am I stronger now than I was before?

10
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:55,317
Or as weak as back then?

11
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:57,417
I don't know for sure.

12
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:01,157
But until I do, my voyage will not end.

13
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:06,340
No matter what's next, I'm
walking straight ahead!

14
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,577
So let's go, there's nothing
that can stop us now!

15
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:17,560
Though times are on our side,
we'll never let it pull us down.

16
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:22,597
And we may fall, but we'll
always keep on standing.

17
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:28,697
There's no way anything will take
what I hold dear away from me.

18
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:33,657
The voices inside me push
me to keep surviving.

19
00:01:33,740 --> 00:01:39,257
I'll go on, I'll get through,
no matter what I gotta do!

20
00:01:39,340 --> 00:01:43,177
The fiercest of the ball can pour upon me.

21
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:48,740
I don't care why in the
world would I turn back?

22
00:01:52,220 --> 00:01:54,277
So let's go!

23
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:57,877
There's nothing that can stop us now!

24
00:01:57,960 --> 00:02:00,177
Though times love on our side?

25
00:02:00,260 --> 00:02:02,837
We'll never let it pull us down.

26
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:04,937
And we may fall.

27
00:02:05,020 --> 00:02:07,817
But we'll always keep on standing.

28
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:10,557
There's no way anything?

29
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:14,077
Will take what I hold dear away from me.

30
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:17,600
I know the future's there for us to see.

31
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:43,800
But we were so close!

32
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:48,900
Oh

33
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:57,820
He's why!

34
00:03:42,020 --> 00:03:44,820
I'm sorry.

35
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:52,160
They got Firefist! He's dead!

36
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:13,460
Strawboy, no!

37
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:16,340
The poor kid's shutting down!

38
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:18,953
He's got to get killed!

39
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:33,530
Akainu!

40
00:04:33,740 --> 00:04:35,480
I won't miss twice!

41
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:37,760
There's no one to save you!

42
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:42,600
It's over, Straw Hat!

43
00:04:50,320 --> 00:04:52,517
I've seen enough death for today.

44
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:54,577
Back off!

45
00:04:54,660 --> 00:04:57,557
Wake up, Luffy!

46
00:04:57,640 --> 00:04:58,977
We have to run!

47
00:04:59,060 --> 00:05:01,560
Move or you're next!

48
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:11,340
Listen, we cannot give in to despair!

49
00:05:13,060 --> 00:05:15,117
Go carry Straw Hat!

50
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:16,700
If you won't run, hurry!

51
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:22,937
We may have lost Ace today, but
he'll live on through Luffy!

52
00:05:23,020 --> 00:05:25,740
You're right, boss!

53
00:05:30,780 --> 00:05:35,637
If Ace can't protect him, then as
his family, we have to step up!

54
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:38,600
Ace is our brother!

55
00:05:39,460 --> 00:05:43,180
Fight like your pride's
on the line in his honor!

56
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:53,160
Pull it together for your
brother's sake, Loopy!

57
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:59,440
When I hold an execution, I make
damn sure to finish the job!

58
00:06:05,580 --> 00:06:07,840
You can't run from me!

59
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:11,520
Look behind you!

60
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:31,320
Oh, my God.

61
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:03,760
Damn, he's mad as hell!

62
00:07:03,920 --> 00:07:05,920
Come on, we gotta get out of here!

63
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:31,540
Ugh!

64
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:00,980
Oh, no!

65
00:08:01,660 --> 00:08:03,120
Oh, no!

66
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:24,360
What are you doing for me?

67
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:07,060
Oh, my God.

68
00:09:13,180 --> 00:09:14,010
Oh!

69
00:09:50,240 --> 00:09:52,340
He's too strong!

70
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:54,000
HQ's done for!

71
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:09,080
Son of a...

72
00:10:11,380 --> 00:10:12,700
Whitefeel!

73
00:10:16,640 --> 00:10:18,500
Admiral Sakazuki!

74
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:25,000
Come on!

75
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:26,000
Come on, help!

76
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:50,150
I...

77
00:10:50,233 --> 00:10:51,340
I think it's stopped.

78
00:10:53,940 --> 00:10:55,180
Damn it, why?

79
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:03,220
The plaza split in half.

80
00:11:03,520 --> 00:11:05,108
We can't reach the pirates.

81
00:11:05,420 --> 00:11:06,361
Awaiting orders.

82
00:11:07,520 --> 00:11:08,897
He's stuck over there.

83
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:10,577
We can't even fight!

84
00:11:10,660 --> 00:11:12,320
But why?

85
00:11:19,340 --> 00:11:22,237
I thought the man was on his last leg.

86
00:11:22,320 --> 00:11:24,438
Where is all this power coming from?

87
00:11:25,180 --> 00:11:26,400
Want more?

88
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:33,297
I am your enemy.

89
00:11:33,380 --> 00:11:35,580
And I alone.

90
00:11:36,260 --> 00:11:40,920
So if you have a resolve to face me, come!

91
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:46,330
Retreat!

92
00:11:46,420 --> 00:11:49,400
Get back to the ship! Hell no!

93
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:52,180
All we can do is honor his wishes.

94
00:11:52,540 --> 00:11:56,300
As his sons, we should be grateful
and hold our heads up high!

95
00:11:56,460 --> 00:11:57,737
Save your tears for later!

96
00:11:57,820 --> 00:11:59,460
Let's move! I'm done!

97
00:11:59,780 --> 00:12:02,000
I can't! Stand up!

98
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:10,080
If a ship can sail, bring it to
the bayhead and line him off!

99
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:12,660
We can still shoot you, dammit!

100
00:12:14,340 --> 00:12:15,800
I'm wasting time!

101
00:12:21,300 --> 00:12:23,160
Salome, take me to Luffy.

102
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:24,674
I fear for his safety.

103
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:33,840
Sorry for disobeying orders, but someone's
got to watch this to the end, Pops.

104
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:39,580
AHHHHH! GAH!

105
00:12:41,140 --> 00:12:45,883
GAH!

106
00:12:53,580 --> 00:12:54,920
GAH! GAH!

107
00:12:58,480 --> 00:12:59,620
Hey, look!

108
00:12:59,820 --> 00:13:01,114
What the hell is that?

109
00:13:02,760 --> 00:13:03,737
It's huge!

110
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:05,657
Whatever it is it can't be good.

111
00:13:05,740 --> 00:13:10,057
Oops they found me
there's someone else too.

112
00:13:10,140 --> 00:13:14,537
There's a whole group of people up
on the scaffold you fellas ain't

113
00:13:14,620 --> 00:13:20,940
very observant are you blackbeard it
seems you've made some new friends.

114
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:25,024
I thought they were locked
up and impelled down.

115
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:28,910
Teach.

116
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:33,197
They were supposed to
be erased from history.

117
00:13:33,280 --> 00:13:35,221
After the crimes they committed,?

118
00:13:35,520 --> 00:13:37,461
even death was too great a mercy!

119
00:13:39,180 --> 00:13:41,886
He's the largest living
creature in the world!

120
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:45,780
The great battleship, San Juan Wolf!

121
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:49,500
Wow, they even know my name.

122
00:13:49,680 --> 00:13:51,280
Well, I'll be...

123
00:13:51,820 --> 00:13:54,080
The corrupt king, Avalopizarro!

124
00:13:54,580 --> 00:13:55,600
Now I'm back!

125
00:13:55,820 --> 00:13:56,800
Now you die!

126
00:13:57,860 --> 00:14:00,340
Heavy drinker, Vasco, shut!

127
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:10,409
I'm gonna go ahead and
kill them all, okay?

128
00:14:10,820 --> 00:14:12,055
Crescent Moon Hunter!

129
00:14:12,160 --> 00:14:13,220
Katarina Devon!

130
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:14,670
Maroon!

131
00:14:15,260 --> 00:14:16,880
You boys want this?

132
00:14:17,060 --> 00:14:17,920
Try me.

133
00:14:18,940 --> 00:14:21,764
And that's the old jail
manager from Impel Down!

134
00:14:22,380 --> 00:14:23,560
Shiryu of the Reign!

135
00:14:24,740 --> 00:14:26,975
They've joined the Blackbeard Pirates!

136
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:28,330
See?

137
00:14:32,700 --> 00:14:34,180
Hey there, pups.

138
00:14:34,560 --> 00:14:37,160
I'm glad I could make it to your funeral.

139
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:42,620
You miss me, you fat bastard.

140
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:59,000
Shit of you.

141
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:00,540
What's going on?

142
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:06,920
What happened at Impelled Down I have a
hunch that Magellan didn't release you?

143
00:15:07,980 --> 00:15:10,140
How did you make it to Marine Ford?

144
00:15:13,140 --> 00:15:15,857
Well old friend maybe
you ought to worry less

145
00:15:15,940 --> 00:15:18,557
about how we got here
and worry more about what

146
00:15:18,640 --> 00:15:25,237
You're going to do now
that we are if you want

147
00:15:25,320 --> 00:15:27,877
to find out more check
out Impelled Down later?

148
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:29,431
That'll give you an idea.

149
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:32,997
By the way, I'm switching sides
in case you couldn't tell.

150
00:15:33,080 --> 00:15:35,198
Figured you might want to know that.

151
00:15:38,220 --> 00:15:39,760
Lead Admiral Sengoku!

152
00:15:40,980 --> 00:15:43,921
I'm sorry I wasn't able
to inform you sooner, sir.

153
00:15:46,420 --> 00:15:49,797
We received a report that the Gates
of Justice opened a second time,

154
00:15:49,880 --> 00:15:52,920
and an unidentified ship
was able to pass through!

155
00:15:53,580 --> 00:15:55,297
So that's how they made it.

156
00:15:55,380 --> 00:15:58,240
But the control room is
under Navy operation.

157
00:15:58,640 --> 00:16:01,060
Nothing else unusual was reported either.

158
00:16:02,060 --> 00:16:04,700
So how could you slip past us undetected?

159
00:16:06,640 --> 00:16:08,405
That's where I'll take credit.

160
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:11,000
Allow me to explain.

161
00:16:12,460 --> 00:16:13,517
Rapscallions that we are,

162
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:16,757
we crashed the party at Impel Down
and picked up your old friend.

163
00:16:16,840 --> 00:16:18,797
Then I thought I'd have a spot of fun and

164
00:16:18,880 --> 00:16:21,557
hypnotize the Navy soldiers
in the control room.

165
00:16:21,640 --> 00:16:25,875
I made them open the Gates of Justice
for any Navy ship that approached.

166
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:30,757
Incidentally, that seems to have helped
a few other rogues get through as well.

167
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:34,657
And since I was considered a navy
ally, I got through just fine.

168
00:16:34,740 --> 00:16:38,697
If it weren't for my title, I couldn't
have made it inside the prison either.

169
00:16:38,780 --> 00:16:43,577
Long story short, being a warlord
made this little operation a cinch.

170
00:16:43,660 --> 00:16:46,020
But now I'm through with you.

171
00:16:48,080 --> 00:16:51,440
You used us just to bolster
the ranks of your crew?

172
00:16:53,460 --> 00:16:56,440
The old soldier finally figured it out!

173
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:59,240
My plan is almost complete now!

174
00:16:59,700 --> 00:17:01,320
You'll see soon enough!

175
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:19,960
Let's finish this, you damn traitor!

176
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:25,360
Dash!

177
00:17:31,660 --> 00:17:33,980
Captain! Incoming!

178
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:56,140
Now that was close.

179
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:59,028
Good to see our reflexes
are still in order.

180
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:14,097
So much for old times.

181
00:18:14,180 --> 00:18:15,780
Guess I can't blame you.

182
00:18:17,520 --> 00:18:21,049
Of all the pirates who have
called the Moby Dick their home,

183
00:18:21,340 --> 00:18:25,800
you're the only one I refuse
to call my son. Teach.

184
00:18:26,120 --> 00:18:31,460
There is only one rule I have on
my ship, and you dared to break it.

185
00:18:31,820 --> 00:18:34,900
You betrayed our trust by
killing your fellow mate.

186
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:37,440
It's time to put an end to this.

187
00:18:37,820 --> 00:18:41,938
You'll pay for 4th Division Commander
Thatcher's death with your life.

188
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:44,780
Mark my words, he will be avenged.

189
00:18:46,540 --> 00:18:48,140
Pops, what are you doing?

190
00:18:49,880 --> 00:18:50,710
Marco!

191
00:18:53,640 --> 00:18:55,320
Let me help you!

192
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:02,460
Listen, you stay out of this one, boy.

193
00:19:02,960 --> 00:19:04,160
But you're hurt!

194
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:06,440
Did you hear me?

195
00:19:10,940 --> 00:19:15,280
Let's get this over with right now. See?

196
00:19:15,780 --> 00:19:16,980
Ha ha ha ha ha!

197
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:19,204
What do you think I'm here for?

198
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:30,750
Uh oh!

199
00:19:31,100 --> 00:19:33,557
What's that black stuff
coming out of his body?

200
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:34,760
Is that... smoke?

201
00:19:51,600 --> 00:19:53,360
Enjoy this black hole.

202
00:20:01,800 --> 00:20:02,630
See?

203
00:20:03,580 --> 00:20:06,760
This Devil Fruit power is
exactly why I killed Fish.

204
00:20:06,960 --> 00:20:08,460
I knew I had to have it.

205
00:20:09,100 --> 00:20:11,340
Dark, dark fruit is real tasty.

206
00:20:11,740 --> 00:20:13,387
Why don't you give it a try?

207
00:20:13,540 --> 00:20:14,370
Why?

208
00:20:14,453 --> 00:20:16,092
Don't worry, there's plenty to go around.

209
00:20:20,140 --> 00:20:21,800
You know there's a pattern.

210
00:20:22,360 --> 00:20:25,948
First Thatch kicks the bucket,
and now Ace has followed suit.

211
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:29,517
All your top underlings seem
to be dropping like flies,

212
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:32,177
and you're too old to do
a damn thing about it.

213
00:20:32,260 --> 00:20:34,437
Good thing I'm no longer under your thumb.

214
00:20:34,520 --> 00:20:37,557
If I hadn't have gotten out when I did,
who knows where I would have ended up.

215
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:39,360
And I'll have you know,

216
00:20:39,600 --> 00:20:43,188
I spared him at Bonnaroo Island
when I could have killed him.

217
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:47,020
I will not stand for this!

218
00:20:48,180 --> 00:20:50,500
Easy now, don't even bother!

219
00:20:51,140 --> 00:20:54,980
Your power won't work against
me, no Devil Fruit power will!

220
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:13,400
This darkness of mine is
pretty handy, ain't it?

221
00:21:13,580 --> 00:21:17,874
I can nullify your fancy little tricks
just like I did with good old Ace.

222
00:21:19,460 --> 00:21:23,660
In other words, no more
earthquakes, not against me!

223
00:21:46,540 --> 00:21:48,920
You're arrogant, a fool.

224
00:21:49,360 --> 00:21:51,900
You were never fit to be in my crew.

225
00:21:55,720 --> 00:21:57,520
Hey, hold on!

226
00:21:58,520 --> 00:21:59,940
Pops, please don't!

227
00:22:00,140 --> 00:22:02,220
I'm your son, Pops! Stop it!

228
00:22:02,520 --> 00:22:04,285
You wouldn't gun your own son!

229
00:22:22,620 --> 00:22:23,997
He did it!

230
00:22:24,080 --> 00:22:25,480
There you go, Pops!

231
00:22:28,220 --> 00:22:29,160
Hey, look!

232
00:22:29,380 --> 00:22:30,740
He's still alive!

233
00:23:01,220 --> 00:23:03,340
Get away from me, you monster!

234
00:23:07,460 --> 00:23:10,000
I said get away from me!

235
00:23:10,820 --> 00:23:12,140
Damn it!

236
00:23:12,400 --> 00:23:14,580
Will you just die already?

237
00:23:22,220 --> 00:23:24,580
No, don't do it!

238
00:23:27,720 --> 00:23:30,360
Finish him off! Hurry!

239
00:24:06,100 --> 00:24:08,480
Come on, Pops!

240
00:24:08,800 --> 00:24:10,100
Please don't die!

241
00:24:17,260 --> 00:24:18,900
What do you mean, Roger?

242
00:24:19,240 --> 00:24:20,420
You're going to die?

243
00:24:21,320 --> 00:24:23,960
Yeah, I could just feel it.

244
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:29,780
Do you want to know how to get to Raptal?

245
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:32,680
I could tell you, if you'd like.

246
00:24:33,200 --> 00:24:34,030
Don't bother.

247
00:24:34,320 --> 00:24:36,379
I've got no interest in that place.

248
00:24:39,300 --> 00:24:42,077
Those world government clowns
don't know what they're doing.

249
00:24:42,160 --> 00:24:45,219
Do you know what they've
been calling me these days?

250
00:24:46,580 --> 00:24:48,540
They call me Gold Roger.

251
00:24:49,580 --> 00:24:50,500
So what?

252
00:24:50,680 --> 00:24:52,177
I thought that was your name.

253
00:24:52,260 --> 00:24:53,777
Do you want to go by something else now?

254
00:24:53,860 --> 00:24:55,480
No, no, you don't get it.

255
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:59,180
My real name is Gold D. Roger.

256
00:25:00,180 --> 00:25:04,180
Every now and then I come across
someone with a D in their name.

257
00:25:08,980 --> 00:25:11,580
Like my crew member, Marshal D. Teach.

258
00:25:12,740 --> 00:25:15,580
So, what does the D stand for?

259
00:25:17,980 --> 00:25:18,810
That?

260
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:20,380
You wanna know, huh?

261
00:25:23,640 --> 00:25:25,080
Fine, fine.

262
00:25:25,420 --> 00:25:26,480
I can tell you.

263
00:25:29,700 --> 00:25:32,580
It's a story from way back when.

264
00:25:38,100 --> 00:25:44,800
Hey I'm out of bullets someone give
me another gun it's not you teach

265
